course: dictionary
lesson: 9878
title: Choosing kind words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tactful person thinks before speaking or acting, so that others are not upset or hurt. Context helps you see this. «When the Rat wakes, his eyes are brown again but he is flat and sad; the tactful Mole chats about the harvest, apples and cosy winter.» The Rat is sad, but the Mole does not talk about his sadness. He talks about cheerful things, so the Rat is not made to feel worse.
explain: Look at what the tactful Mole does next. «The tactful Mole brought a pencil and paper.» He does not say, "You look miserable." He gives the Rat something useful to do, and the Rat starts scribbling poetry. Tactful is about kindness in both words and actions, and about choosing the right moment.
explain: Tactful has an opposite, tactless, which means not careful about other people's feelings. In Alice, many creatures are very tactless and rude, which makes the story funny for the reader, but in real life a tactless remark can hurt someone. A good check is to ask: would this words make my friend feel better or worse?
fact: Tactful means careful to say and do things in a way that does not upset or hurt others.
fact: A tactful remark is kind and careful about other people's feelings.
fact: Tactful choosing the right moment and the right words, rather than saying the first thing that comes into your head.
fact: The opposite of tactful is tactless.
fact: «Tactful» can describe a person, a remark or an action.
exercise: «When the Rat wakes, he is flat and sad; the tactful Mole chats about the harvest, apples and cosy winter.» What does tactful mean? | Quick to win every game | Rude and loud | *Careful to say things kindly, so others are not upset | Very tall
exercise: The Mole chats about apples instead of asking why the Rat is sad. Which word describes the Mole? | *Tactful | Angry | Greedy | Tactless
exercise: Which word is the opposite of tactful? | Careful | *Tactless | Kind | Gentle
test: Find and copy one word from «The tactful Mole brought a pencil and paper» that describes the Mole's kind, careful manner. | pencil | Mole | paper | *tactful
test: Why is it tactful for the Mole to leave a pencil rather than say, "You look miserable"? | Because pencils are expensive | *Because it helps the Rat without hurting his feelings | Because the Mole is in a hurry | Because it makes the Rat cry
exam: Which sentence shows tactful behaviour? | Shout at the team when they lose | Tell your friend her drawing is ugly | *Tell your friend kindly that the colours are lovely, and suggest one small change | Laugh at a friend's mistake in front of the class
